and castle in Guernsey, and former tidal island, also known as Cornet Rock or Castle Rock. Its importance was as a defence not only of the island, but of the roadstead. In 1859, it became part of one of the breakwaters of Guernsey's main harbour, St Peter Port harbour.","wpu":"Castle Cornet","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Castle_Cornet%2C_Guernsey.jpg/960px-Castle_Cornet%2C_Guernsey.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Royal Guernsey Militia Regimental Museum","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":49.453011,"lo":-2.526758,"d":686,"w":"https://museums.gov.gg/rgm"},{"n":"Hauteville House","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":49.451296,"lo":-2.537657,"d":687,"h":"We-Su 10:00-16:00; Mo,Tu off","wp":"en:Hauteville House","wd":"Q1591410","ad":"38 Hauteville","ds":"Hauteville House is a house in St. Peter Port, Guernsey. Between 1856 and 1870, French writer Victor Hugo lived here during his exile from France.","wpu":"Hauteville House","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Hauteville_House_Victor_Hugo_in_Guernsey.jpg/960px-Hauteville_House_Victor_Hugo_in_Guernsey.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Royal Guernsey Light Infantry Museum","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":49.453043,"lo":-2.526664,"d":689},{"n":"Grange Lodge Hotel","g":"sights","k":"hotel","la":49.456257,"lo":-2.545733,"d":852,"wifi":1},{"n":"Guernsey underground military museum","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":49.448207,"lo":-2.531219,"d":998,"w":"http://lavalette.uk/"},{"n":"German Naval Signals HQ","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":49.461148,"lo":-2.546431,"d":1009,"h":"Mo-Su 12:30-16:30","wd":"Q130265445"},{"n":"Premier Inn","g":"sights","k":"hotel","la":49.468308,"lo":-2.538244,"d":1294,"f":["wc","ac"],"wifi":1},{"n":"Bellegreve Bay","g":"sights","k":"beach","la":49.470055,"lo":-2.530372,"d":1475},{"n":"Chateau de Marais","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":49.471833,"lo":-2.538587,"d"